Mutant: the rule for transactions sent again starts from the header of the last segment. Must fail: a writer opened on a spool continues after its last indexed transaction, with the final_lsn and end LSN of its record; a writer opened on a spool skips its last transaction sent again and appends the next one after it.
Apply from the repository root with git apply, and never commit it applied.

--- a/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
+++ b/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
@@ -2144,7 +2144,7 @@
 		.segment = tail->segment,
 		.relationLog = { .fd = -1 },
 		.nextSeq = tail->last.seq + 1,
-		.lastFinalLSN = tail->last.finalLSN,
+		.lastFinalLSN = tail->header.lastFinalLSN,
 		.lastEndLSN = tail->last.endLSN,
 		.completeSize = tail->last.endOffset
 	};
